==German==
[[Image:MexicanChairs.jpg|thumb|225px|Stühle in Mexiko — Chairs in Mexico.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|stuol|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|stōlaz|lang=de}}. Cognate with Dutch {{term|stoel|lang=nl}}, English {{term|stool|lang=en}}, Swedish {{term|stol|lang=sv}}; ultimately from {{proto|Indo-European|steh₂-|lang=de}} and thus related to {{term|stehen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʃtuːl/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Stuhl.OGG|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=m|genitive=Stuhls|genitive2=Stuhles|plural=Stühle}}

# a [[chair]] (to sit on)
#: ''Ich hab die ganze Zeit auf meinem '''Stuhl''' gesessen!'' — I have sat on my chair all the time!
# a [[chair]] (professorship)
#: ''Professor Martin wurde überraschend auf den '''Stuhl''' berufen.'' — Surprisingly, Professor Martin received the professorship.
# (euphemism, mainly used in medical professions) [[feces]], [[stool]]
#: ''Herr Urkwicz hatte heute wieder sehr weichen '''Stuhl'''.'' — Today Mr Urkwicz had again very soft feces.

